    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an AUDIT log line on successful owner creation, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI kept the logic in its own single-responsibility unit rather than inlining it into the controller:\n\n**New file \u2014 `rest/audit/OwnerAuditLogger.java`**: a small `@Component` that owns audit-trail emission for owner lifecycle events. It logs to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger via `created(Owner)`, formatting the id, customer code, and registration date.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**: injected `OwnerAuditLogger` and call `ownerAuditLogger.created(owner)` immediately after `saveOwner(owner)`. That placement matters \u2014 `registrationDate` and the generated `id` are only resolved once the entity is persisted (`registrationDate` is finalized in the `@PrePersist` hook, rolling forward to a business day), so logging after the save captures the actual stored values.\n\nThe resulting line (e.g. `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-18`) contains all three fields as substrings, which is exactly what the `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` check asserts via `AuditLogCapture`.",
